Catalyst plugin is under review process and can be changed in the future.

The first implementation is done by François Mazen in https://github.com/francois-kitware/pdi in the branch catalyst-plugin

The caltalyst plugin used in this demo is based on a fork
https://github.com/Yushan-Wang/pdi_dev/tree/numpex-septembre-2025-demo


Complilation and execution:

1. compilation of catalyst and paraview:

https://kitware.github.io/paraview-catalyst/guide/getting-started.html

# Remark: The catalyst and paraview need to be compile with MPI support
# Remark: If you want to used live option of catalyst, you need to compile paraview with the GUI
# Remark: For catalyst plugin, the python library mumpy and mpi4py are needed
# Remark: The demo has been tested with Catalyst 2.0 and Paraview 6.0.0 or Paraview 5.13.2

2. compilation of PDI:

You need to clone the branch "numpex-septembre-2025-demo" of the fork of Yushan: https://github.com/Yushan-Wang/pdi_dev/tree/numpex-septembre-2025-demo
You need to compile PDI with the following option (the last option is needed for compile the catalyst example)

-DBUILD_CATALYST_PLUGIN=ON -DBUILD_PYTHON=ON -DBUILD_TESTING=ON

and export the following two variables:

export catalyst_DIR=path_to_install_catalyst/lib/cmake/catalyst-2.0
export Catalyst_DIR=path_to_install_catalyst/lib/cmake/catalyst-2.0
export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=$LD_LIBRARY_PATH:path_to_install_catalyst/install_catalyst/lib


```bash
cd path_to_pdi_root_repository
mkdir build
cd build

export catalyst_DIR=path_to_install_catalyst/lib/cmake/catalyst-2.0
export Catalyst_DIR=path_to_install_catalyst/lib/cmake/catalyst-2.0
export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=$LD_LIBRARY_PATH:path_to_install_catalyst/install_catalyst/lib

cmake -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=../install -DBUILD_CATALYST_PLUGIN=ON -DBUILD_PYTHON=ON -DBUILD_TESTING=ON ..
make
make install
```

# Remark: The used of catalyst_DIR and Catalyst_DIR will be removed when catalyst plugin will be merged with the main branch of PDI.

3. execution of demo

You need to export and to source the following lines

# execution
export CATALYST_IMPLEMENTATION_NAME=paraview
export CATALYST_IMPLEMENTATION_PATHS=path_to_install_paraview/lib/catalyst

# python venv
source $HOME/local_paraview_6.0.0_catalyst_2.0/python_env_catalyst/bin/activate
# pdi environnement
source path_to_install_pdi/share/pdi/env.bash

# update python path

export PYTHONPATH=path_to_install_catalyst/lib/python3.**/site-packages:$PYTHONPATH
export PYTHONPATH=path_to_install_paraview/lib/python3.**/site-packages:$PYTHONPATH

Here, `3.**` correspond to your python version.

# remark: If you used a python venv environement, you need to pass
export PYTHONPATH=path_to_my_venv/lib/python3.**/site-packages:$PYTHONPATH

```bash
mkdir build
cd build
cmake ..

mpirun -np 4 ./demo_catalyst config.yml
```
